      "title": "Recap: the A, P, and E sites",
      "narration": "Quick recap of the three sites. A is where new tRNAs come in. They stay if the anticodon matches. P is where the peptide bond forms. E is where empty tRNAs leave. Watch one full round. In at A. Bond at P. Out from E. Like a factory line: in, join, out. tRNAs enter at A, the peptide bond forms at P, and empty tRNAs leave from E. Let's see what you remember.",
